# NV scoreboard机制

ref:[TRACKING REGISTER USAGE DURING MULTTHREADED PROCESSING USING A SCOREBOARD HAVING SEPARATE MEMORY REGIONS AND STORING SEQUENTIAL REGISTER SIZE INDICATORS]

**本专利中关于指令目标寄存器记录在scoreboard的时机是在发射后,并且发射后不会给I-Buffer中同线程的后序指令补充依赖,可能存在数据冒险.因为指令发射后去获取操作数后执行,该过程不保证按照发射顺序执行,所以发射后指令会乱序执行,遗漏指令依赖会导致数据冒险.**

**理论上应该在指令进入I-Buffer前就将其目标寄存器记录在scoreboard中,因为I-Buffer中指令已经在等待mask归0后发射(乱序执行),所以后序指令应该和I-Buffer中同线程的指令检测依赖.**

## fetch和issue过程

**SM主要包含取指和发射的dispatch、操作数存储的GRF和执行算术、访存指令的不同pipeline.**

FIG. 2 illustrates one of the processing units 124 in additional detail. The processing unit illustrated in FIG. 2, referenced herein as 200, is representative of any one of the processing units 124 shown in FIG. 1. The processing unit 200 includes an instruction dispatch unit 212 for issuing an instruction to be executed by the processing unit 200, a register file 214 that stores the operands used in executing the instruction, and a pair of execution pipelines 222, 224. The first execution pipeline 222 is configured to carry out math operations, and the second execution pipeline 224 is configured to carry out memory access operations. In general, the latency of instructions executed in the second execution pipeline 224 is much higher than the latency of instructions executed in the first execution pipeline 222. When the instruction dispatch unit 212 issues an instruction, the instruction dispatch unit 212 sends pipeline configuration signals to one of the two execution pipelines 222, 224. If the instruction is of the math type, the pipeline configuration signals are sent to the first execution pipeline 222. If the instruction is of the memory access type, the pipeline configuration signals are sent to the second execution pipeline 224. The execution results of the two execution pipelines 222, 224 are written back into the register file 214.

**dispatch中I-buffer中有24个栏目slot,缓存24个不同warp/线程的指令序列,每个栏目容纳2条指令;**

**每条指令包含1个6bit的mask表示该指令是否依赖线程内前序指令的结果.**

**当I-buffer中存在空白栏目,则fetch单元调度1个warp并根据其nPC从I-cache中取指.**

**指令被fetch后,经过译码和ScoreBoard处理,得到译码信息(warp/线程信息、branch等)和数据依赖mask后一并缓存在I-Buffer.**

**ScoreBoard处理将指令的源寄存器编号、目标寄存器编号和ScoreBoard中记录的执行中指令的目标寄存器编号比较,得到指令的依赖情况mask.**

**指令缓存在I-Buffer前,将其目标寄存器记录在ScoreBoard中,因为在以后fetch的指令视角中该指令是前序执行的,即便尚未发射也需要对其检测依赖.**

FIG. 3 is a functional block diagram of the instruction dispatch unit 212 of the instruction processing section 200. The instruction dispatch unit 212 includes an instruction buffer 310 with a plurality of slots. The number of slots in this exemplary embodiment is 24 and each slot can hold up to two instructions and a multi-bit dependency mask for each of the instructions. The multi-bit dependency mask for an instruction provides an indication as to whether the instruction needs to use (depends on) a register that is currently busy. If any one of the slots has a space for another instruction, a fetch 312 is made from memory into an instruction cache 314. After the fetch 312, the instruction undergoes a decode 316 and scoreboard processing 321. During the scoreboard processing 321, register identifiers (IDs) of source and destination registers specified in the instruction are compared with the register IDs stored in a scoreboard memory 322, and a multi-bit value that represents the aggregate comparison result is generated as an output. This output is added to the instruction buffer 310 as the multi-bit dependency mask along with the instruction. In addition, the register ID of the destination register specified in the instruction is added to the scoreboard memory 322. Additional details of scoreboard processing 321 are provided below with reference to FIG. 7.

**dispatch单元中的issue单元检查I-Buffer中指令是否依赖执行中(in flights)的指令(mask≠0),并将无依赖的指令发射到GRF获取操作数后执行.**

**发射前会检测ScoreBoard中该线程/warp的分区是否存在空位来记录发射指令的目标寄存器,若存在空位则发射并在ScoreBoard中记录目标寄存器(???应该在指令进入I-Buffer前就在ScoreBoard中记录其目标寄存器???),否则说明当前线程达到设定的ILP上限,等待出现空位后发射.**

The instruction dispatch unit 212 further includes an issue logic 320. The issue logic 320 examines the instructions and their multi-bit dependency masks stored in the instruction buffer 310 and issues an instruction out of the instruction buffer 310 that is not dependent on any of the instructions in flight (e.g., an instruction having a dependency mask equal to zero), provided that there is available memory space in the scoreboard memory 322 to store the register ID of a destination register specified in the instruction. If not, the issue logic 320 does not issue the instruction until memory space in the scoreboard memory 322 becomes available. In conjunction with the issuance out of the instruction buffer 310, the issue logic 320 sends pipeline configuration signals to the appropriate execution pipeline.

